TITLE:: PianoRoll
SUMMARY:: Piano-roll view for MIDI recording and note editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PianoRollSidebar, Classes/PianoRollTimeline, Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/Metronome, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter, Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/DeleteCommand, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/LegatoCommand, Classes/RightCommand, Classes/SnapCommand, Classes/TransposeCommand, Classes/WriteCommand

DESCRIPTION::
LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows recorded notes as a piano roll. Its root LINK::Classes/View:: uses a vertical layout: an embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: at the top, and a horizontal layout below containing a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: (timeline plus note canvas) and a fixed LINK::Classes/PianoRollSidebar:: on the right. The sidebar shows the loop length from LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: once both loop markers have been set, and, when exactly one note is selected, that note's CODE::midinote::, CODE::amp::, and any non-timing keys stored on its event. It embeds LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline:: for the beat strip above the roll (left/right clicks set loop bounds; Shift+left sets playback; see LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline::). It listens for MIDI note-on and note-off events (when not in dev mode) and draws LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: entries as LINK::Classes/BorderView:: regions. LINK::#-stopRecording:: frees the recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s and updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes. Keyboard shortcuts are dispatched via a LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: passed in at construction.

SUBSECTION:: Keyboard editing
Focus the note area after clicking it:

TABLE::
## Keys || Behaviour
## 1–4 || Assign part on selected notes
## Escape || Focus the command prompt
::

Edits update the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: sequence and are allowed during playback. LINK::#-startRecording:: starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome::; LINK::#-stopRecording:: stops it. Note operations such as amp, delete, left, legato, right, snap, transpose, and write are invoked through the embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::. The prompt is constructed with LINK::Classes/AmpCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LeftCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/RightCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/SnapCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/TransposeCommand#*new::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand#*new:: (passing the optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument::). Ambient parameters supply CODE::selectedNotes::, CODE::allNotes::, CODE::loopStart::, CODE::loopEnd::, and CODE::midiChannel::. CODE::loopStart:: and CODE::loopEnd:: are nil until both loop markers have been set. The CODE::delete:: command removes every selected note from the roll and from the sequence. The CODE::left:: and CODE::right:: commands move every selected note by the typed CODE::resolution::. The CODE::transpose:: command adds the typed integer to every selected note's MIDI note number. The CODE::write:: command inserts a CODE::~seq.addMidiSequence:: line via LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument#-insertPattern::.

SUBSECTION:: Navigation
The mouse wheel scrolls the roll vertically. Shift and the mouse wheel scroll it horizontally; wheel-up moves toward earlier beats. Ctrl and the mouse wheel zoom horizontally through four steps: half, the default scale, double, and quadruple. Wheel-up zooms in. The beat under the pointer stays put. Dragging on empty roll space draws a rectangle and selects the notes inside it. Clicking a note selects that note. Without Ctrl, either gesture clears the previous selection first. Ctrl+drag and Ctrl+click add to the selection. Clicking empty space clears the selection unless Ctrl is held.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for embedding.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for layout.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for colours.

ARGUMENT:: tempoClock
The LINK::Classes/TempoClock:: used for timing when recording.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When true, skips MIDI setup and fills fake notes for development.

ARGUMENT:: keyRouter
The LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: used for Record-view keyboard shortcuts.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
An optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: used to write pattern source. Pass CODE::nil:: when embedding without a document.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: commandPrompt
The embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: instance used for command input.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::.

METHOD:: playLoop
Starts playback of the recorded sequence via the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::. Returns false and posts a warning if no notes have been recorded.

METHOD:: selectedNotes
Returns an LINK::Classes/Array:: of currently selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

METHOD:: startRecording
Arms MIDI recording (or fills fake notes in dev mode) and starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome::.

METHOD:: stopLoop
Stops playback via the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::.

METHOD:: stopRecording
Stops recording, stops the LINK::Classes/Metronome::, frees recording LINK::Classes/MIDIdef::s, and updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes (loop bounds plus LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers#-playheadTime_:: at the loop start beat).

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyNoteEdits, prAssignPartIfSelected, prDeleteNote, prRefreshSidebar, prRegisterKeyHandlers, prSelectedNotes
